+```
+
+`git diff --check` on the UI11 source, test, and plan files emitted no output and exited 0. UI11 adds no user-facing sentences or engine behavior.
+
+## Review challenge
+
+The prior mark looked too large after the transparent-canvas trim, so its fitted frame was reduced from 92% to 86%. The old menu-logo outline pixel assertion referred to the previous raster mark; it was replaced by checks of the new vector output for theme distinction, transparency, neutral grayscale, and badge/plain rendering. The Dock test bounds-checks scale and the signature. The independent reviewer found no issues: the Dock mark is scaled without clipping; the menu symbol is monochrome vector art with the theme-aware glass gradient and badge; tests match the rendering, with no stale assertions or unrelated package changes.
+
+## Commit
+
+Git metadata is read-only in this environment. `docs/plan/reports/patches/UI11.patch` was verified to apply after UI10 and reproduce the six scoped paths. The exact paths and commit message are in the UI11 Ready to commit entry in `docs/plan/STATUS.md`. No commit or push was attempted.
+
+## Fixture launch follow-up
+
+The first UI11 fixture launch crashed while `BatonBrand.nativeIcon()` requested `Bundle.module`: `/private/tmp/BatonFixture.app/Contents/Resources` contained the executable target's `Baton_Baton.bundle`, but not the UI target's `Baton_BatonUI.bundle`. I copied the already-built `app/.build/debug/Baton_BatonUI.bundle` into the app's `Contents/Resources` and relaunched the same review app with `--review-window`. LaunchServices returned success; no later Baton crash report appeared in DiagnosticReports when checked. No project source, fixture content, settings, or real chat was changed.
+
+The desktop automation surface was unavailable to this turn, so I could not independently confirm the visible window or menu bar. Rendered snapshots remain the visual verification for UI11.
